Unreleased
==========

Symbolic trie
-------------

- Added an in-memory, 8-way symbolic-trie index with configurable leaf
  capacity, sampled root splitting, and entropy × variance-based splits.
- Stores MBRs and selects split dimensions across the full transform word
  (up to 64 dimensions); record lower bounds use the leading 16 dimensions.
- Supports SAX, SFA, and SPARTAN words, including integer input files and
  query-specific symbolic lower-bound lookup tables.
- Uses node-MBR pruning plus best-first leaf scans, ordered by record lower
  bounds, with exact-distance early abandonment.
- Provides batch and single-query parallel modes with configurable worker and
  queue counts, plus construction, coverage, and per-phase query timings.

iSAX
----

- Added dynamic, variance-driven root-cardinality splitting for symbolic
  transforms and support for SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words.
- Added full-word node MBR pruning and transform-specific lower bounds,
  including SIMD-capable exact-distance paths where available.
- Improved parallel index construction and hybrid query scheduling, including
  configurable worker/queue counts and robust queue ownership.
- Unified iSAX and trie benchmark summaries, CSV logs, coverage reporting,
  construction timings, and optional per-phase query profiling.
